  "tagline": "Columnar streaming storage for Flink with primary-key tables and tiering into the lakehouse.",
  "description": "Fluss is a streaming storage layer designed for real-time analytics with Apache Flink, positioned as a table-oriented alternative to Kafka for analytical pipelines. Log tables store append-only streams in an Arrow-based columnar format with projection pushdown, and primary-key tables support upserts, changelog generation and low-latency key lookups for lookup joins. A tiering service continuously compacts data into Paimon, Iceberg, Hudi or Lance so streaming and lakehouse reads can be unioned. Open-sourced by Alibaba in late 2024, it entered the Apache Incubator in 2025 and is now a top-level project; 1.0.0 shipped in September 2026.",
